// backend_demo_lobby: lobbies against the in-memory test backend (`fake://`). Nobody real is on the other side, nothing is saved between
// runs and no two browsers ever meet (run it natively with `--backend <server>` against a lobby-enabled server to meet real players: see
// "Lobbies" in docs/20_data_formats.md). Three lobbies are seeded: row 1 "Demo lobby" (host Ada, 1/4), row 2 "Quick game" (host Grace,
// 3/4) and row 3 "Demo lobby" (host Linus, full 2/2). The other members are scripted, so you can see every event:
//   - a lobby YOU create: Ada joins on the 2nd check-in (about 20 s), Grace on the 4th, and the newest rival leaves on the 5th;
//   - Ada's lobby (row 1) when you join it: Grace joins on the 2nd check-in and Ada PRESSES START on the 4th (you get lobby.started);
//   - Grace's lobby (row 2) when you join it: Grace LEAVES on the 6th check-in (you get lobby.closed:host_left).
// A check-in happens every 10 seconds. Try the failure paths too (add them to the endpoint): "fake://?fail=join_full" (every join answers
// `full`), "fake://?fail=gone", "fake://?fail=start" (Start fails), "fake://?fail=list" (the list fails), "fake://?fail=heartbeat" (the
// waiting room loses contact: "Reconnecting...", and after a minute lobby.closed:server), "fake://?fail=sign_in", "fake://?fail=unreachable"
// and "fake://?latency=120" (about two seconds to answer).
// A real server also needs its `server_key` (here, or `NAKAMA_SERVER_KEY` for a native `--backend` run, which never uses this file's key),
// and its admin must list this game and switch lobbies on (`ironhold backend config` writes `Lobbies` and `lobby_names` into the server
// config; a server that was not regenerated answers `not_enabled`). Each real player needs their own computer or user account.
BackendConfig(
    schema_version: 1,
    // Namespace on a shared server: [a-z0-9_], 1-32 characters. Defaults to project_id when omitted.
    game_id: "backend_demo_lobby",
    endpoint: "fake://",
    // Lobbies must be declared, like leaderboards: a server is provisioned for what a project says it uses.
    features: [Lobbies],
    // The only names `CreateLobby(name: ...)` may use (1-32 printable ASCII characters). A closed list, not free text.
    lobby_names: ["Demo lobby", "Quick game"],
)
